# What `require` answers is what the variable of the file holds, which begins as undefined. Nobody finds that undefined where the body stores to the variable on the one way that it begins with,
# and whoever reads the variable comes behind the store: at the head of the body nothing has run yet; further down, the file has to be seen whole.
# RUN: valueflow-why values=f0:v2 values=f0:v5 values=f0:v8 values=f0:v11 values=f0:v14 values=f0:v17 values=f0:v20 values=f0:v25 values=f0:v28 values=f0:v31
# at the head
# CHECK: values=f0:v2
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 1 members: f12
# further down, behind a require of its own
# CHECK: values=f0:v5
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 1 members: f13
# on a cycle
# CHECK: values=f0:v8
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 2 members: primitive0 f14
# asked for by a request that may come while the body runs
# CHECK: values=f0:v11
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 2 members: primitive0 f16
# under a handler
# CHECK: values=f0:v14
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 2 members: primitive0 f17
# read by a function of the file
# CHECK: values=f0:v17
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 2 members: primitive0 f18
# its module object is in hand
# CHECK: values=f0:v20
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 2 members: primitive0 f19
# read by a function that no require stands in front of
# CHECK: values=f0:v25
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 2 members: primitive0 f20
# under a test
# CHECK: values=f0:v28
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 2 members: primitive0 f21
# read by the body ahead of the store
# CHECK: values=f0:v31
# CHECK: operand 0 {{*}} 2 members: primitive0 f22

